Reason:
The code only verifies that the firmware buffer is at least 16 bytes, but does not check that the declared data stream length (`file_length`) does not exceed the remaining buffer size (`size - 16`). This allows a malformed firmware with an artificially large `file_length` to cause a buffer overrun when accessing `data[16 + i]`.

